long to; and load a workspace by slug with the visible channel list plus embedded `read_state`. It locks `WorkspaceObj`, the initial `ChannelObj` shape used by later channel APIs, the SQLite schema for workspaces/members/channels, and the REST contracts the SPA shell (MARATHON-16) and members/channels tasks (MARATHON-6/7) consume.\\n\\n**Revision (needs-revision feedback):** `read_state` entries use the **full** `ReadStateEntry` shape shared with `GET /api/channels/{id}/read` (MARATHON-11): `{channel_id, last_read_seq, unread_count, mention_count}`. Empty `[]` until messages/read APIs write rows is fine; when [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"../../tmp/loom-list.json","matches":[{"lineNumber":60,"content":"    \"design\": \"# MARATHON-5 — Workspaces: create, list, detail, auto #general\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nThis task adds the workspace tenancy root for Huddle: authenticated callers can create a workspace (unique kebab `slug`, display `name`, creator as `owner`, default `join_mode=open`), which atomically provisions the public `#general` channel and membership rows; list workspaces they own or belong to; and load a workspace by slug with the visible channel list plus embedded `read_state`. It locks `WorkspaceObj`, the initial `ChannelObj` shape used by later channel APIs, the SQLite schema for workspaces/members/channels, and the REST contracts the SPA shell (MARATHON-16) and members/channels tasks (MARATHON-6/7) consume.\\n\\n**Revision (needs-revision feedback):** `read_state` entries use the **full** `ReadStateEntry` shape shared with `GET /api/channels/{id}/read` (MARATHON-11): `{channel_id, last_read_seq, unread_count, mention_count}`. Empty `[]` until messages/read APIs write rows is fine; wh [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":325,"content":"    \"id\": \"MARATHON-22\",","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":326,"content":" 