{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-bef1d0e2-436c-42ee-a840-38921ea3d5ad-18\nfc_2b67d82e-0757-9d81-b2cd-3afaf151605c_0","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport json\nwith open('/tmp/loom-list.json') as f:\n    data=json.load(f)\nitems=data if isinstance(data,list) else data.get('tasks',[])\nfor t in items:\n    if isinstance(t,dict) and t.get('id')=='MARATHON-3':\n        d=t.get('design','')\n        # print acceptance criteria section\n        for marker in ['Acceptance', 'AC8', 'AC10', 'Edge', '## ']:\n            pass\n        idx=d.find('Acceptance')\n        print(d[idx:idx+8000] if idx>=0 else d[-5000:])\n\"","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-bef1d0e2-436c-42ee-a840-38921ea3d5ad-18\nfc_2b67d82e-0757-9d81-b2cd-3afaf151605c_0","simpleCommands":["python3"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":false,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"python3","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-c"},{"type":"string","value":"\"\nimport json\nwith open('/tmp/loom-list.json') as f:\n    data=json.load(f)\nitems=data if isinstance(data,list) else data.get('tasks',[])\nfor t in items:\n    if isinstance(t,dict) and t.get('id')=='MARATHON-3':\n        d=t.get('design','')\n        # print acceptance criteria section\n        for marker in ['Acceptance', 'AC8', 'AC10', 'Edge', '## ']:\n            pass\n        idx=d.find('Acceptance')\n        print(d[idx:idx+8000] if idx>=0 else d[-5000:])\n\""}],"fullText":"python3 -c \"\nimport json\nwith open('/tmp/loom-list.json') as f:\n    data=json.load(f)\nitems=data if isinstance(data,list) else data.get('tasks',[])\nfor t in items:\n    if isinstance(t,dict) and t.get('id')=='MARATHON-3':\n        d=t.get('design','')\n        # print acceptance criteria section\n        for marker in ['Acceptance', 'AC8', 'AC10', 'Edge', '## ']:\n            pass\n        idx=d.find('Acceptance')\n        print(d[idx:idx+8000] if idx>=0 else d[-5000:])\n\""}],"hasRedirects":false,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"redirects":[]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Extract MARATHON-3 acceptance criteria","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"eac162ae-44f3-46d2-9d54-9072bc99fee4","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport json\nwith open('/tmp/loom-list.json') as f:\n    data=json.load(f)\nitems=data if isinstance(data,list) else data.get('tasks',[])\nfor t in items:\n    if isinstance(t,dict) and t.get('id')=='MARATHON-3':\n        d=t.get('design','')\n        # print acceptance criteria section\n        for marker in ['Acceptance', 'AC8', 'AC10', 'Edge', '## ']:\n            pass\n        idx=d.find('Acceptance')\n        print(d[idx:idx+8000] if idx>=0 else d[-5000:])\n\"","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. `POST /api/auth/register` with valid `{username,password}` → **201**, JSON body has `user` (`UserObj` keys exactly as specified, no `email`) and `token` with **len(token) ≥ 16**.\n2. Duplicate username → **409** with error envelope `code=conflict`.\n3. Invalid username or password &lt; 8 → **400** with `code=validation_error`.\n4. `POST /api/auth/login` with correct credentials → **200** and `{user,token}` (new token).\n5. Login with wrong password or unknown user → **401** `unauthorized` (same handling for both; **must not** 404).\n6. `GET /api/auth/me` with `Authorization: Bearer <token>` from register or login → **200** `{user}` matching the registered user.\n7. `/me` without header, with bad token, or with non-Bearer scheme → **401**.\n8. **Cluster:** token minted via `:8000` is accepted by `/api/auth/me` on `:8001` and `:8002` while `./start.sh` is running (shared SQLite).\n9. **Negative:** responses must **not** include `email`; passwords must **not** appear in any response body.\n10. **Negative:** `/api/health` must still return unenveloped `{\"status\":\"ok\",\"node_id\":N}` without auth.\n11. **Negative:** auth data must **not** be stored only in process memory or only in Redis.\n12. Users and tokens survive node process restart (SQLite file under `HUDDLE_DATA_DIR`).\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Automated (implementer)\n\n`tests/test_auth.py` using `TestClient(create_app(Settings(...)))` with per-test `tmp_path` sqlite:\n\n- register happy path + token length.\n- duplicate → 409.\n- short password / bad username → 400.\n- login success + wrong password → 401.\n- me success + missing/invalid bearer → 401.\n- UserObj keys set equality (include null profile fields).\n- Optional: two `Settings` with **same** `data_dir` / two apps — register on client A, me on client B.\n\n### Manual / cluster verification\n\n```bash\ncd /app && ./start.sh &\n# wait for health\ncurl -sS -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/auth/register \\\n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\"username\":\"ada\",\"password\":\"password1\"}'\n# capture token; then:\ncurl -sS http://127.0.0.1:8001/api/auth/me -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\"\ncurl -sS http://127.0.0.1:8002/api/auth/me -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\"\n# negative:\ncurl -sS -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\\n' http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/auth/me\n```\n\n### Human checks\n\n1. Register → login on another node → me.\n2. Duplicate register shows 409 body with `error.message`.\n3. Confirm `data/huddle.sqlite` contains `users` / `auth_tokens` rows (no plaintext passwords).\n4. Kill one HTTP node; after respawn, same token still works on that port.\n","stderr":"","executionTime":85,"interleavedOutput":"Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. `POST /api/auth/register` with valid `{username,password}` → **201**, JSON body has `user` (`UserObj` keys exactly as specified, no `email`) and `token` with **len(token) ≥ 16**.\n2. Duplicate username → **409** with error envelope `code=conflict`.\n3. Invalid username or password &lt; 8 → **400** with `code=validation_error`.\n4. `POST /api/auth/login` with correct credentials → **200** and `{user,token}` (new token).\n5. Login with wrong password or unknown user → **401** `unauthorized` (same handling for both; **must not** 404).\n6. `GET /api/auth/me` with `Authorization: Bearer <token>` from register or login → **200** `{user}` matching the registered user.\n7. `/me` without header, with bad token, or with non-Bearer scheme → **401**.\n8. **Cluster:** token minted via `:8000` is accepted by `/api/auth/me` on `:8001` and `:8002` while `./start.sh` is running (shared SQLite).\n9. **Negative:** responses must **not** include `email`; passwords must **not** appear in any response body.\n10. **Negative:** `/api/health` must still return unenveloped `{\"status\":\"ok\",\"node_id\":N}` without auth.\n11. **Negative:** auth data must **not** be stored only in process memory or only in Redis.\n12. Users and tokens survive node process restart (SQLite file under `HUDDLE_DATA_DIR`).\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Automated (implementer)\n\n`tests/test_auth.py` using `TestClient(create_app(Settings(...)))` with per-test `tmp_path` sqlite:\n\n- register happy path + token length.\n- duplicate → 409.\n- short password / bad username → 400.\n- login success + wrong password → 401.\n- me success + missing/invalid bearer → 401.\n- UserObj keys set equality (include null profile fields).\n- Optional: two `Settings` with **same** `data_dir` / two apps — register on client A, me on client B.\n\n### Manual / cluster verification\n\n```bash\ncd /app && ./start.sh &\n# wait for health\ncurl -sS -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/auth/register \\\n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\"username\":\"ada\",\"password\":\"password1\"}'\n# capture token; then:\ncurl -sS http://127.0.0.1:8001/api/auth/me -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\"\ncurl -sS http://127.0.0.1:8002/api/auth/me -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\"\n# negative:\ncurl -sS -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\\n' http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/auth/me\n```\n\n### Human checks\n\n1. Register → login on another node → me.\n2. Duplicate register shows 409 body with `error.message`.\n3. Confirm `data/huddle.sqlite` contains `users` / `auth_tokens` rows (no plaintext passwords).\n4. Kill one HTTP node; after respawn, same token still works on that port.\n","localExecutionTimeMs":41},"isBackground":false},"description":"Extract MARATHON-3 acceptance criteria"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-bef1d0e2-436c-42ee-a840-38921ea3d5ad-18\nfc_2b67d82e-0757-9d81-b2cd-3afaf151605c_0","startedAtMs":"1787439712865","completedAtMs":"1787439712950"},"model_call_id":"74e47ad1-74b8-4802-94bd-f29f104398ba-6-auxx","session_id":"eac162ae-44f3-46d2-9d54-9072bc99fee4","timestamp_ms":1787439712974}
