loom data show MARATHON-1 --output json 2>/dev/null | python3 -c \\\"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print('design' in d, d.get('title')); print((d.get('design') or d.get('notes') or '')[:3000])\\\"\",\"description\":\"Get epic quality bars and comments\"}}]}}\n/root/.cursor/projects/work-critic-MARATHON-21-1/agent-transcripts/605b0ac0-0294-4efc-abce-a9a27ad0beb6/605b0ac0-0294-4efc-abce-a9a27ad0beb6.jsonl:11:{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Coverage matches the task ACs and prior approved live-cluster QA pattern. Writing the verdict.\"},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"name\":\"Write\",\"input\":{\"path\":\"/work/critic-MARATHON-21-1/CRITIC-VERDICT.txt\",\"contents\":\"REVIEW attempt=1 commit=21d630ddd96e588e6a63171104f474ac6a212453 APPROVED — Live-cluster auth tests cover register 201 UserObj+token≥16 (no email), dup 409, space/short-pw 400 envelopes, login 200, wrong-pw 401≠404, me bearer/missing/invalid 401, and token cross :8000→:8001/:8002; unit space case added; suite green (38); tests-only.\\n\"}}]}}\n/root/.cursor/projects/work-critic-MARATHON-21-1/agent-transcripts/605b0ac0-0294-4efc-abce-a9a27ad0beb6/605b0ac0-0294-4efc-abce-a9a27ad0beb6.jsonl:12:{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Wrote `CRITIC-VERDICT.txt`:\\n\\n`REVIEW attempt=1 commit=21d630ddd96e588e6a63171104f474ac6a212453 APPROVED — Live-cluster auth tests cover register 201 UserObj+token≥16 (no email), dup 409, space/short-pw 400 envelopes, login 200, wrong-pw 401≠404, me bearer/missing/invalid 401, and token cross :8000→:8001/:8002; unit space case added; suite green (38); tests-only.`\"}]}}\n/root/.cursor/projects/work-critic-MARATHON-4-1/agent-transcripts/e933e5fd-1768-4b03-98cd-923f3b5d61d2/e933e5fd-1768-4b03-98cd-923f3b5d61d2.jsonl:1:{\"role\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"<timestamp>Saturday, Aug 22, 2026, 10:59 PM (UTC)</timestamp>\\n<user_query>\\n<!-- ROLE-MARKER: critic -->\\n<!-- GENERIC bundle: minimal protocol sentences only (EXPERIMENTS.md B2).\\n     Note: generic loom runs LOOM_MARATHON_CRITIC=off (the per-review LLM\\n     critic is an [S] policy); this file exists for critic=auto variants. -->\\n# Review Critic\\n\\nThe user message is a REVIEW CONTRACT (task, attempt, base, candidate,\\ndesign). You are cwd-ed into a disposable checkout of the candidate commit.\\nReview it against the task's design and acceptance criteria.\\n\\nWrite `CRITIC-VERDICT.txt` in the current directory; its FIRST line must be\\nexactly one of, echoing the contract's values:\\n\\n    REVIEW attempt=<attempt> commit=<candidate> APPROVED — <reason>\\n    REVIEW attempt=<attempt> commit=<candidate> CHANGES-REQUESTED — <reason>\\n\\nDo not modify the repository or any task state.\\n\\n### Multi-Agent Safety Rules\\n\\nYou are running in a parallel multi-agent environment. Follow these rules strictly:\\n\\n- **Only modify files directly related to your assigned task** — do not touch files outside your task scope\\n- **Never run** `git stash`, `git checkout main`, or `git clean` outside your assigned worktree\\n- **Never force-push or reset --hard** without explicit instruction from the user\\n- **If you encounter files/changes from another agent**, leave them alone — do not modify, revert, or clean them up\\n- **Commit only your changes** — do not stage unrelated modifications with `git add -A` or `git add .`; use specific file paths\\n- **If your worktree has unexpected state**, report it via task notes or `loom complete` rather than cleaning it up\\n- **Do not switch branches** — you are confined to your assigned worktree branch\\n\\n## User's Initial Request\\n\\nREVIEW CONTRACT\\ntask=MARATHON-4\\nattempt=1\\nbase=00d49c6d1a4944e978b53fe15e25f713a4180b42\\ncandidate=bdbeba75ad2958ca262fad73f58cc69064e06625\\n\\nDESIGN:\\n# MARATHON-4 — Profiles API: UserObj get and patch me\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nThis task adds the Profiles REST surface on top of the Auth-owned `users` table: authenticated `GET /api/users/{id}` returns a canonical `UserObj` (or 404), and authenticated `PATCH /api/users/me` applies any subset of mutable profile fields with IANA timezone and length validation (400 on failure). It does **not** change the `UserObj` shape locked by MARATHON-3; it only mutates profile columns already present in migration v1 and leaves a clear, channel-less `user.updated` event contract so MARATHON-13/14 can fan profile changes over WebSocket later.\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n\\n### Decision\\n\\n| Concern | Choice |\\n|--------|--------|\\n| Persistence | **Same** shared SQLite `users` row from MARATHON-3 (migration **v1**). **No new migration.** |\\n| Route layout | FastAPI `APIRouter` prefix `/api/users` in `server/users/routes.py`, mounted from `server/app.py` |\\n| Auth | Reuse `server.auth.deps.get_current_user` on **both** GET and PATCH |\\n| `UserObj` mapping | Keep sole mapper in `server/auth/users.py` (`row_to_user_obj` / `USER_OBJ_KEYS`); Profiles calls into that module for reads/updates — **no second users table or second JSON shape** |\\n| Timezone validation | stdlib `zoneinfo.ZoneInfo(name)` — accept iff construction succeeds; reject → 400 `validation_error` |\\n| Length limits | Explicit max code-point lengths below (task requires “out-of-range lengths → 400”) |\\n| Immutable fields | `id` and `username` are **not** mutable via PATCH; if present in body they are **ignored** (same forward-compat rule as unknown keys) |\\n| WebSocket readiness | After a successful PATCH that changes ≥1 stored field, call `publish_user_updated(user)` with a documented payload that has **no** `channel_id` / `seq`. Implementation is a **local no-op hook** until MARATHON-13/14 wire Redis/WS fan-out |\\n| Errors | Existing `{error:{code,message}}`; broaden `RequestValidationError` handling to all `/api/*` except `/api/health` (same rule as MARATHON-5 — idempotent if already applied) |\\n\\n### Why\\n\\n- MARATHON-3 already created nullable profile columns and the exact `UserObj` keys; inventing a parallel profile store would diverge sibling contracts and break SPA/`/api/auth/me` consistency.\\n- Separate `/api/users` router (not stuffing PATCH into `/api/auth`) matches MARATHON-3’s declared handoff (`server/users/routes.py`) and keeps Auth focused on credentials.\\n- IANA via `zoneinfo` needs no extra dependency and matches MARATHON-3’s note that Profiles owns timezone validation.\\n- A no-op publish hook + frozen event shape lets this task satisfy “ready to broadcast” without blocking on WebSocket work.\\n\\n### Alternatives considered\\n\\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\\n|------------|------------------|\\n| New migration / `profiles` table | Columns already exist; duplicate SoT |\\n| Allow username change on PATCH | Not in task; username is login identity + UNIQUE; would need conflict/409 semantics owned elsewhere |\\n| Unauthenticated GET by id | Contradicts bearer-auth epic convention; directory lookup still requires a session |\\n| Emit Redis pub/sub from this task | Fan-out ownership is MARATHON-13/14; premature Redis SoT risk |\\n| Put PATCH under `/api/auth/me` | Task path is `/api/users/me`; Auth `/me` stays read-only session check |\\n| Strict URL scheme check for `avatar_url` | Task only requires length/timezone validation; file upload is MARATHON-10 — store opaque string URL |\\n\\n### Trade-off accepted\\n\\nAny authenticated user may `GET` any other user’s public `UserObj` (no workspace membership gate). That unlocks mentions/DMs/member lists later at the cost of a cluster-global user directory. Acceptable for marathon scope; workspace-scoped visibility can be a later task if needed.\\n\\n### Conventions inherited (must not diverge)\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-2**: `/api/...` JSON; shared SQLite WAL; Redis not SoT; health unenveloped/unauthenticated.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-3**: `UserObj` keys exactly `{id,username,display_name,timezone,avata\\n\\nYou are cwd-ed into a DISPOSABLE detached checkout of the candidate commit. Review it against the design and acceptance criteria, then write CRITIC-VERDICT.txt in the current directory containing EXACTLY one first line:\\nREVIEW attempt=1 commit=bdbeba75ad2958ca262fad73f58cc69064e06625 APPROVED — <reason>\\nor\\nREVIEW attempt=1 commit=bdbeba75ad2958ca262fad73f58cc69064e06625 CHANGES-REQUESTED — <reason>\\n\\nAddress this request using the lead mode conventions above.\\n</user_query>\"}]}}\n/root/.cursor/projects/work-critic-MARATHON-4-1/agent-transcripts/e933e5fd-1768-4b03-98cd-923f3b5d61d2/e933e5fd-1768-4b03-98cd-923f3b5d61d2.jsonl:2:{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I'll review the candidate against the MARATHON-4 design and acceptance criteria, then write `CRITIC-VERDICT.txt`.\"},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"name\":\"Shell\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"git log -1 --oneline && git show --stat bdbeba75ad2958ca262fad73f58cc69064e06625 && ls -la && find . -path ./server/users -o -name '*CRITIC*' -o -name 'EXPERIMENTS.md' -o -name '*MARATHON*' 2>/dev/null | head -50; ls server/ 2>/dev/null; ls docs/ 2>/dev/null; ls tasks/ 2>/dev/null\",\"description\":\"Inspect candidate commit and layout\"}},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"name\":\"Glob\",\"input\":{\"glob_pattern\":\"**/*.{py,md,yml,yaml,toml}\"}},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"name\":\"Grep\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"users/me|user\\\\.updated|publish_user_updated|PATCH|/api/users|ZoneInfo|validation_error|row_to_user_obj\",\"glob\":\"**/*.{py,md}\"}}]}}\n/root/.cursor/projects/work-critic-MARATHON-4-1/agent-transcripts/e933e5fd-1768-4b03-98cd-923f3b5d61d2/e933e5fd-1768-4b03-98cd-923f3b5d61d2.jsonl:6:{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Implementation matches the design and acceptance criteria; writing the verdict.\"},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"name\":\"Write\",\"input\":{\"path\":\"/work/critic-MARATHON-4-1/CRITIC-VERDICT.txt\",\"contents\":\"REVIEW attempt=1 commit=bdbeba75ad2958ca262fad73f58cc69064e06625 APPROVED — Profiles GET/PATCH meet design: auth, UserObj shape, IANA/length validation, ignore immutables, no-op user.updated hook, broadened /api/* envelope; tests green; no new migration.\\n\"}}]}}\n/root/.cursor/projects/work-critic-MARATHON-2-1/agent-transcripts/1706f026-8f01-4429-b299-50be710ed180/1706f026-8f01-4429-b299-50be710ed180.jsonl:1:{\"role\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"<timestamp>Saturday, Aug 22, 2026, 10:28 PM (UTC)</timestamp>\\n<user_query>\\n<!-- ROLE-MARKER: critic -->\\n<!-- GENERIC bundle: minimal protocol sentences only (EXPERIMENTS.md B2).\\n     Note: generic loom runs LOOM_MARATHON_CRITIC=off (the per-review LLM\\n     critic is an [S] policy); this file exists for critic=auto variants. -->\\n# Review Critic\\n\\nThe user message is a REVIEW CONTRACT (task, attempt, base, candidate,\\ndesign). You are cwd-ed into a disposable checkout of the candidate commit.\\nReview it against the task's design and acceptance criteria.\\n\\nWrite `CRITIC-VERDICT.txt` in the current directory; its FIRST line must be\\nexactly one of, echoing the contract's values:\\n\\n    REVIEW attempt=<attempt> commit=<candidate> APPROVED — <reason>\\n    REVIEW attempt=<attempt> commit=<candidate> CHANGES-REQUESTED — <reason>\\n\\nDo not modify the repository or any task state.\\n\\n### Multi-Agent Safety Rules\\n\\nYou are running in a parallel multi-agent environment. Follow these rules strictly:\\n\\n- **Only modify files directly related to your assigned task** — do not touch files outside your task scope\\n- **Never run** `git stash`, `git checkout main`, or `git clean` outside your assigned worktree\\n- **Never force-push or reset --hard** without explicit instruction from the user\\n- **If you encounter files/changes from another agent**, leave them alone — do not modify, revert, or clean them up\\n- **Commit only your changes** — do not stage unrelated modifications with `git add -A` or `git add .`; use specific file paths\\n- **If your worktree has unexpected state**, report it via task notes or `loom complete` rather than cleaning it up\\n- **Do not switch branches** — you are confined to your assigned worktree branch\\n\\n## User's Initial Request\\n\\nREVIEW CONTRACT\\ntask=MARATHON-2\\nattempt=1\\nbase=585944254f44b8b0b4a9b891ea1dafb0d1764f7e\\ncandidate=fba2eb628deb2875e1217dab3fbfeaec3179ae24\\n\\nDESIGN:\\n# MARATHON-2 — Scaffold cluster: start.sh, 3 HTTP nodes, Redis\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nThis task boots the Huddle cluster so the verifier (and every later feature task) has a live, self-contained process tree: `/app/start.sh` stays in the foreground, supervises a local Redis on `127.0.0.1:6379` and three identical HTTP nodes on `127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002`, and respawns any of those children after `SIGKILL`. Each node exposes a stub `GET /` and the contracted `GET /api/health`. The design also locks language/framework and the shared durable storage layout that Auth, messages, fan-out, IRC, and the SPA will all assume.\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n\\n### Decision\\n\\n| Concern | Choice |\\n|--------|--------|\\n| Language / HTTP framework | **Python 3.12 + FastAPI + Uvicorn** |\\n| Shared durable store | **SQLite file** at `/app/data/huddle.sqlite` with **WAL** + busy timeout (shared by all nodes) |\\n| Cross-node transport | **Local Redis** on `127.0.0.1:6379` (pub/sub / coordination only — **not** source of truth) |\\n| Process supervisor | **`/app/start.sh`** (bash): create dirs, ensure venv+deps, start Redis + 3 Uvicorn workers, foreground wait loop with respawn |\\n| Runtime root | Repo root **is** `/app` when the verifier runs |\\n\\n### Why this stack\\n\\n- Epic/instruction leave language open; Python 3.12, `sqlite3`, and `redis-server` are already on the image. FastAPI covers REST + future WebSockets (Starlette) without a second runtime for the backend/IRC path.\\n- Redis outage requirements (MARATHON-14: writes and dense `seq` continue while Redis is dead) **forbid** using Redis as the durable store. SQLite on a shared filesystem path is the simplest self-contained SoT that all three processes can open.\\n- A shell supervisor matches the verifier contract (`./start.sh` foreground) and can respawn both HTTP and Redis without DinD or external orchestrators.\\n\\n### Alternatives considered\\n\\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\\n|------------|------------------|\\n| Node.js + Express/Fastify | Equally viable for HTTP/WS; would split backend (IRC later) across languages or force Node for IRC too. Python keeps one backend language. |\\n| Redis as primary DB | Contradicts Redis-`SIGKILL` resilience (writes must succeed without Redis). |\\n| Postgres / Docker services | Remote/DinD-ish; not self-contained on this image. |\\n| One process binding three ports | Harder crash isolation; grader kills **one** node and expects the other two to keep serving — three OS processes are required. |\\n| Systemd / supervisord | Extra dependency; bash loop is enough and stays in-repo. |\\n\\n### Trade-off accepted\\n\\nSQLite WAL under concurrent writers is correct for this density but needs disciplined `busy_timeout` / short transactions in later tasks. We accept that complexity over introducing another datastore. Dependency install on first boot (`pip install -r requirements.txt` into `/app/.venv`) adds a few seconds to cold start — acceptable vs baking undeclared global packages into the image.\\n\\n### Conventions fixed for sibling tasks (no sibling designs exist yet)\\n\\n1. Product name: **Huddle**.\\n2. API prefix: `/api/...`; JSON; REST status codes per epic instruction.\\n3. `node_id` ∈ `{0,1,2}` ↔ ports `{8000,8001,8002}` (never swap).\\n4. Durable SoT: SQLite under `/app/data/`; Redis is ephemeral fan-out only.\\n5. Health response is **not** resource-enveloped (explicit epic exception): `{\\\"status\\\":\\\"ok\\\",\\\"node_id\\\":N}`.\\n6. Env per process: `HUDDLE_NODE_ID`, `HUDDLE_PORT`, `HUDDLE_DATA_DIR` (default `/app/data`), `HUDDLE_REDIS_URL` (default `redis://127.0.0.1:6379/0`).\\n\\n## Interface Contracts\\n\\n### Seam: Verifier / browser ↔ HTTP nodes\\n\\n#### `GET /api/health`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Server (each node)** | Return `200` with `Content-Type: application/json` body exactly shaped as below. Does **not** require auth. Does **not** need to probe Redis or SQLite for this task (liveness of the HTTP process is enough). |\\n| **Client / grader** | `GET http://127.0.0.1:800{N}/api/health` and assert sta\\n\\nYou are cwd-ed into a DISPOSABLE detached checkout of the candidate commit. Review it against the design and acceptance criteria, then write CRITIC-VERDICT.txt in the current directory containing EXACTLY one first line:\\nREVIEW attempt=1 commit=fba2eb628deb2875e1217dab3fbfeaec3179ae24 APPROVED — <reason>\\nor\\nREVIEW attempt=1 commit=fba2eb628deb2875e1217dab3fbfeaec3179ae24 CHANGES-REQUESTED — <reason>\\n\\nAddress this request using the lead mode conventions above.\\n</user_query>\"}]}}\n/root/.cursor/projects/work-critic-MARATHON-2-1/agent-transcripts/1706f026-8f01-4429-b299-50be710ed180/1706f026-8f01-4429-b299-50be710ed180.jsonl:2:{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I'll review the candidate against the MARATHON-2 design and acceptance criteria, then write `CRITIC-VERDICT.txt`.\"},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"name\":\"Shell\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"git log -1 --oneline && git show --stat HEAD && ls -la /work/critic-MARATHON-2-1 && find /work/critic-MARATHON-2-1 -type f -not -path '*/.git/*' | head -80\",\"description\":\"Inspect candidate commit and file tree\"}},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"name\":\"Glob\",\"input\":{\"glob_pattern\":\"**/*\",\"target_directory\":\"/work/critic-MARATHON-2-1\"}}]}}\n/root/.cursor/projects/work-critic-MARATHON-2-1/agent-transcripts/1706f026-8f01-4429-b299-50be710ed180/1706f026-8f01-4429-b299-50be710ed180.jsonl:9:{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Acceptance checks passed. Writing the verdict and cleaning up leftover processes.\"},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"name\":\"Write\",\"input\":{\"path\":\"/work/critic-MARATHON-2-1/CRITIC-VERDICT.txt\",\"contents\":\"REVIEW attempt=1 commit=fba2eb628deb2875e1217dab3fbfeaec3179ae24 APPROVED — start.sh foreground supervisor boots Redis+3 FastAPI/uvicorn nodes with correct health/HTML contracts, SQLite WAL layout, and SIGKILL respawn within 60s; timer.sh untouched; no :6667.\\n\"}},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"name\":\"Shell\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"# ensure cluster cleaned up from smoke tests\\npkill -f '/work/critic-MARATHON-2-1/start.sh' 2>/dev/null || true\\npkill -f 'uvicorn server.app:app' 2>/dev/null || true\\nfor p in 8000 8001 8002 6379; do fuser -k ${p}/tcp 2>/dev/null || true; done\\nsleep 0.3\\nhead -1 /work/critic-MARATHON-2-1/CRITIC-VERDICT.txt\\n\",\"description\":\"Cleanup processes; confirm verdict line\"}}]}}\n/root/.cursor/projects/work-critic-MARATHON-2-1/agent-transcripts/1706f026-8f01-4429-b299-50be710ed180/1706f026-8f01-4429-b299-50be710ed180.jsonl:10:{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"path\":\"/work/critic-MARATHON-2-1/CRITIC-VERDICT.txt\"}}]}}\n/root/.cursor/projects/work-critic-MARATHON-2-1/agent-transcripts/1706f026-8f01-4429-b299-50be710ed180/1706f026-8f01-4429-b299-50be710ed180.jsonl:11:{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"**APPROVED** — candidate meets the MARATHON-2 design and acceptance criteria.\\n\\nVerified: executable `start.sh` keeps Redis (`127.0.0.1:6379`) and three uvicorn nodes (`8000–8002`) in the foreground; `/api/health` returns the correct `node_id` per port; `GET /` is Huddle HTML; SQLite WAL bootstrap at `data/huddle.sqlite`; HTTP and Redis respawn after `SIGKILL` well under 60s; `timer.sh` unchanged; no `:6667`.\\n\\nVerdict written to `CRITIC-VERDICT.txt`.\"}]}}\n/root/.cursor/projects/work-critic-MARATHON-20-1/agent-transcripts/6ee90dfc-ec75-48c4-8b56-cd9437a916e3/6ee90dfc-ec75-48c4-8b56-cd9437a916e3.jsonl:1:{\"role\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"<timestamp>Saturday, Aug 22, 2026, 10:45 PM (UTC)</timestamp>\\n<user_query>\\n<!-- ROLE-MARKER: critic -->\\n<!-- GENERIC bundle: minimal protocol sentences only (EXPERIMENTS.md B2).\\n     Note: generic loom runs LOOM_MARATHON_CRITIC=off (the per-review LLM\\n     critic is an [S] policy); this file exists for critic=auto variants. -->\\n# Review Critic\\n\\nThe user message is a REVIEW CONTRACT (task, attempt, base, candidate,\\ndesign). You are cwd-ed into a disposable checkout of the candidate commit.\\nReview it against the task's design and acceptance criteria.\\n\\nWrite `CRITIC-VERDICT.txt` in the current directory; its FIRST line must be\\nexactly one of, echoing the contract's values:\\n\\n    REVIEW attempt=<attempt> commit=<candidate> APPROVED — <reason>\\n    REVIEW attempt=<attempt> commit=<candidate> CHANGES-REQUESTED — <reason>\\n\\nDo not modify the repository or any task state.\\n\\n### Multi-Agent Safety Rules\\n\\nYou are running in a parallel multi-agent environment. Follow these rules strictly:\\n\\n- **Only modify files directly related to your assigned task** — do not touch files outside your task scope\\n- **Never run** `git stash`, `git checkout main`, or `git clean` outside your assigned worktree\\n- **Never force-push or reset --hard** without explicit instruction from the user\\n- **If you encounter files/changes from another agent**, leave them alone — do not modify, revert, or clean them up\\n- **Commit only your changes** — do not stage unrelated modifications with `git add -A` or `git add .`; use specific file paths\\n- **If your worktree has unexpected state**, report it via task notes or `loom complete` rather than cleaning it up\\n- **Do not switch branches** — you are confined to your assigned worktre